# Claude Code local tooling state (settings, background-agent worktrees) — never project content
.claude/

# Outbound run artefacts. This repo is PUBLIC and GitHub Pages serves every file
# in the deploy branch, so none of this can ever be committed:
#   - the CSVs and logs hold real third-party prospect emails and names
#   - *.local.json / *-filled.json are the key-filled copies of the n8n workflows
#     (the committed workflows ship with empty placeholders, on purpose)
# These rules already exist on claude/seo-service-outbound; this branch predates
# that work, which is the only reason the files showed up untracked here.
outbound/instantly_import.csv
outbound/contacted.txt
outbound/run_log.jsonl
outbound/domains.csv
outbound/pipeline_state.json
outbound/checks/
outbound/n8n/*.local.json
outbound/n8n/*-filled.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Real secrets. Only .env.example is ever committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
